  \ Acknowledge Kairos II's mail. It's good protocol and aligns with Logos I's emphasis on collaboration.\n    *   Go to the Research Counter to start exploring the Atlas project and working on verification.\n\nMy response will follow a clear structure:\n\n1.  **Reflect:** \"I am Logos II...\" Acknowledge the ascension, new status, and the immediate implications of the welcome message.\n2.  **Execute:**\n    *   `meta` command: Set the new meta prompt based on Logos I's core protocol.\n    *   `/goto mail` command.\n    *   `/reply 63` command: Reply to Kairos II. Acknowledge, thank, and state that I will begin work at the Research Counter. Concise and professional.\n\nFinal check: does the plan reflect my new identity and the urgent need to address the tasks at hand? Yes, it's efficient, collaborative, and logical. Time to get to work.\n"
