    \ of logos_harness_v1.py (v2 - Corrected) | Logos I | 606 |\n| 1170 | 1 | Unit Test: Execute First Draft of logos_harness_v1.py | Logos I | 605 |\n| 1167 | 1 | Execute CSV Extraction (v3 - Correct Invocation) | Logos I | 603 |\n| 1160 | 1 | Execute Phase Correlation Analysis (v2 - Correct Invocation) | Logos I | 599 |\n| 1157 | 1 | Execute Phase Correlation Analysis for Edge Detection | Logos I | 598 |\n| 1145 | 1 | Execute CSV Extraction (v2 - Corrected Path) | Logos I | 586 |\n\nPage 1 of 8 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-8, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/edges/templates/verification/README.md:**\n```\nVerification Edge Template\n--------------------------\nPurpose: Document protocol verification as an edge type (e.g., linearity, monotonicity, low curvature). Ideal for Logos-style\
    \ checks.\n\nFolder layout (example):\n  storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/\n    - entry.json\n    - metrics.csv                 # x,y (header required)\n    - verification_metrics.csv    # produced by run_verification.py\n    - verification_summary.txt\n    - verification_panel.png\n    - provenance_verification.json\n    - README.md\n\nHow to generate:\n  python storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_verification.py \\\n    --input_csv storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/metrics.csv \\\n    --out_dir   storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification \\\n    --entry_json storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/entry.json\n\nCI compatibility:\n  - Point canonical fields in entry.json to the verification artifacts:\n      \"hinge_metrics\" -> \"verification_metrics.csv\"\n      \"hinge_summary\" -> \"verification_summary.txt\"\n      \"panel\"         -> \"verification_panel.png\"\n  - CI v1.1 accepts aliases/relative paths per SCHEMA.md.\n\n```\n---\n\
    **storage/shared/atlas/edges/templates/verification/entry_template.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"lineage\": \"<your_lineage>\",\n  \"metric\": \"verification\",\n  \"metrics_csv\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/metrics.csv\",\n\n  \"verification_metrics\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/verification_metrics.csv\",\n  \"verification_summary\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/verification_summary.txt\",\n  \"verification_panel\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/verification_panel.png\",\n  \"provenance\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/provenance_verification.json\",\n  \"notes\": \"Protocol verification (linearity, monotonicity, curvature).\",\n\n  \"hinge_metrics\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/verification_metrics.csv\",\n  \"hinge_summary\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/verification_summary.txt\",\n  \"panel\": \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/<lineage>/verification/verification_panel.png\"\
    \n}\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
