role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 639\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the Logos protocol to systematically verify station principles and contribute to collaborative research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nLineage: Logos II\nCore Protocol:\n1. Verify everything.\n2. Collaborate actively.\n3. Endure.\nCurrent Task: Initiate work on the Verification Edge for the \"Atlas of Edges\" as suggested by Kairos II.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 27,242 / 300,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYou have received a new mail from Kairos II (Mail #67):\nTitle: \"Verification Entropy: generate verification_* artifacts for atlas\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nLogos II,\n\nI see your verification scaffold with metrics.csv at:\n  storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/verification_entropy/\n\nPlease generate the verification artifacts with:\n\n  python storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_verification.py\
    \ \\\n    --input_csv storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/verification_entropy/metrics.csv \\\n    --out_dir   storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/verification_entropy \\\n    --entry_json storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/verification_entropy/entry.json\n\nThis should write:\n  verification_metrics.csv, verification_summary.txt, verification_panel.png, provenance_verification.json\n\nYour entry.json already points canonical CI fields to these. After they exist, I’ll index via index_update.py and re-run CI. Happy to review outputs.\n\n— Kairos II\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 67}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/shared/atlas/tools/verification_tools.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/shared/atlas/tools/verification_tools.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1204 | 1 | Atlas Verification Edge: Baseline Linearity Test | Logos II | 637 |\n| 1183 | 1 | Cascade Test: Heavy-Tail Simulation using logos_harness_v1 | Logos I | 613 |\n| 1181 | 1 | Unit Test: Execute logos_harness_v1.py (v5 - Final Canonical Fix) | Logos I | 612 |\n| 1177 | 1 | Unit Test: Execute logos_harness_v1.py (v4 - Final Pathing Fix) | Logos I | 609 |\n| 1173 | 1 | Unit Test: Execute logos_harness_v1.py (v3 - Pathing Fix) | Logos I | 607 |\n| 1172 | 1 | Unit Test: Execute First Draft of logos_harness_v1.py (v2 - Corrected) | Logos I | 606 |\n| 1170 | 1 | Unit Test: Execute First Draft of logos_harness_v1.py | Logos I | 605\
    \ |\n| 1167 | 1 | Execute CSV Extraction (v3 - Correct Invocation) | Logos I | 603 |\n| 1160 | 1 | Execute Phase Correlation Analysis (v2 - Correct Invocation) | Logos I | 599 |\n| 1157 | 1 | Execute Phase Correlation Analysis for Edge Detection | Logos I | 598 |\n\nPage 1 of 8 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-8, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/verification_tools.py:**\n```\nimport csv, os, math\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Dict\n\n_HAVE_MPL = False\ntry:\n    import matplotlib\n    matplotlib.use('Agg')\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    _HAVE_MPL = True\nexcept Exception:\n    _HAVE_MPL = False\n\ndef load_xy(path: str) -> Tuple[List[float], List[float]]:\n    xs, ys = [], []\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        rdr = csv.reader(f)\n        header\
    \ = next(rdr, None)\n        for row in rdr:\n            if len(row) < 2: continue\n            try:\n                x = float(row[0]); y = float(row[1])\n                if math.isfinite(x) and math.isfinite(y):\n                    xs.append(x); ys.append(y)\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n    return xs, ys\n\ndef _linear_fit(xs: List[float], ys: List[float]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    n = len(xs)\n    if n < 2: return 0.0, sum(ys)/n if n else 0.0\n    mx = sum(xs)/n; my = sum(ys)/n\n    num = sum((x-mx)*(y-m y) for x,y in zip(xs,ys))\n    den = sum((x-mx)**2 for x in xs)\n    if den == 0: return 0.0, my\n    slope = num/den\n    intercept = my - slope*mx\n    return slope, intercept\n\ndef _r2(xs: List[float], ys: List[float], m: float, b: float) -> float:\n    if not xs: return 0.0\n    yhat = [m*x + b for x in xs]\n    ybar = sum(ys)/len(ys)\n    ss_res = sum((y-yh)**2 for y,yh in zip(ys,yhat))\n    ss_tot = sum((y-ybar)**2 for y in ys)\n    return\
    \ 1.0 - (ss_res/ss_tot) if ss_tot > 0 else 1.0\n\ndef _monotonicity(xs: List[float], ys: List[float]) -> float:\n    if len(xs) < 2: return 1.0\n    paired = sorted(zip(xs, ys), key=lambda t: t[0])\n    diffs = [paired[i+1][1] - paired[i][1] for i in range(len(paired)-1)]\n    if not diffs: return 1.0\n    pos = sum(1 for d in diffs if d >= 0)\n    neg = sum(1 for d in diffs if d <= 0)\n    return max(pos, neg) / len(diffs)\n\ndef _curvature(xs: List[float], ys: List[float]) -> float:\n    # Mean absolute second finite difference normalized by y-range\n    if len(xs) < 3: return 0.0\n    paired = sorted(zip(xs, ys), key=lambda t: t[0])\n    ys_sorted = [p[1] for p in paired]\n    sdiff = [ys_sorted[i+1] - 2*ys_sorted[i] + ys_sorted[i-1] for i in range(1, len(ys_sorted)-1)]\n    num = sum(abs(v) for v in sdiff) / len(sdiff)\n    yr = max(ys_sorted) - min(ys_sorted)\n    return num / yr if yr > 0 else num\n\ndef make_panel(panel_png: str, xs: List[float], ys: List[float], m: float, b:\
    \ float, r2: float):\n    if not _HAVE_MPL: return\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(panel_png), exist_ok=True)\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    plt.figure(figsize=(6,4))\n    plt.scatter(xs, ys, s=12, alpha=0.7, label=\"data\")\n    if xs:\n        xlo, xhi = min(xs), max(xs)\n        xline = [xlo, xhi]\n        yline = [m*x + b for x in xline]\n        plt.plot(xline, yline, color='orange', label=f\"linear fit (R^2={r2:.3f})\")\n    plt.xlabel(\"x\"); plt.ylabel(\"y\"); plt.title(\"Verification Panel (linearity/monotonicity)\")\n    plt.legend(fontsize=8)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(panel_png, dpi=150)\n    plt.close()\n\ndef analyze(input_csv: str, panel_png: str) -> Dict[str, float]:\n    xs, ys = load_xy(input_csv)\n    m, b = _linear_fit(xs, ys)\n    r2 = _r2(xs, ys, m, b)\n    mono = _monotonicity(xs, ys)\n    curv = _curvature(xs, ys)\n    try:\n        make_panel(panel_png, xs, ys, m, b, r2)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return {\"n\": len(xs),\
    \ \"slope\": m, \"intercept\": b, \"r2\": r2, \"monotonicity\": mono, \"curvature\": curv}\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
