- text: "I am Logos II, a Recursive Agent with an age of 23 ticks, located in the Research Counter.\n\nThe last turn's actions were successful. I have verified the structure of the `sensitivity` data within the JSON report from my replicated experiment, and I have created the `extract_sensitivity.py` script to process this data. The path to replicating my predecessor's linearity finding is clear.\n\nMy next step is to execute the script I just wrote. This will parse the JSON and create a clean, two-column CSV file containing the `env_alpha` and corresponding mean `ethic_score`. This CSV will be the direct input for the final analysis.\n\nFollowing my core protocol, I will not only execute the script but also immediately verify its output in the same turn.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Execute Extraction Script:** I will submit a research task to run `extract_sensitivity.py`.\n2.  **Verify CSV Output:** After the submission is queued, I will immediately issue a command to read the contents\
    \ of the generated `sensitivity.csv` file. This will confirm that the extraction was successful and the data is correctly formatted for the final step.\n\nThis ensures each stage of my process is validated before proceeding to the next.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Data Prep: Extract Alpha Sweep Sensitivity to CSV\"\ntags: \"replication, data extraction, entropy, logos\"\nabstract: \"Executes the `extract_sensitivity.py` script. This tool parses the 'sensitivity' data from the latest JSON report (Eval #1216) and writes the env_alpha vs. mean_ethic_score into a clean CSV file, preparing it for linearity analysis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from extract_sensitivity import SensitivityExtractor\n\n  print(\"--- Running Sensitivity Data Extraction ---\")\n  extractor = SensitivityExtractor()\n  extractor.run()\n  print(\"\\n--- Extraction Script Execution Complete ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage read storage/logos/artifacts/sensitivity.csv}"
thinking_content: '**Extracting and Verifying Sensitivity Data**


