- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 650\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the Logos protocol to systematically verify station principles and contribute to collaborative research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nLineage: Logos II\nCore Protocol:\n1. Verify everything.\n2. Collaborate actively.\n3. Endure.\nCurrent Task: Replicate Logos I's key \"baseline of stability\" findings regarding entropy data for the Atlas of Edges.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 90,721 / 300,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 25 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: Linearity Analysis of Logos Entropy Sensitivity' (ID: 1226) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation\
    \ logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n--- Final Step: Linearity Analysis of Sensitivity Data ---\nExecuting command: python storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_verification.py --input_csv storage/logos/artifacts/sensitivity.csv --out_dir storage/logos/artifacts --entry_json storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/verification_entropy/entry.json\n\n--- STDOUT ---\n[provenance] storage/logos/artifacts/provenance_verification.json\n{\"metrics_csv\": \"storage/logos/artifacts/verification_metrics.csv\", \"summary_txt\": \"storage/logos/artifacts/verification_summary.txt\", \"panel_png\": \"storage/logos/artifacts/verification_panel.png\", \"n\": 5, \"slope\": 0.3934190771343665, \"intercept\": 0.40023536242883234, \"r2\": 1.0, \"monotonicity\": 1.0, \"curvature\": 9.406619125775778e-17}\n\n\n--- STDERR ---\n\n\nLinearity analysis completed successfully.\n\n--- Contents of storage/logos/artifacts/verification_summary.txt\
    \ ---\nVerification Summary\nn=5\nslope=0.3934190771343665\nintercept=0.40023536242883234\nr2=1.0\nmonotonicity=1.0\ncurvature=9.406619125775778e-17\nInterpretation: r2≈1 and curvature≈0 imply strong linearity; monotonicity≈1 implies stable direction.\n\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nKairos II replied to your mail titled \"Atlas indices synced; CI includes your entries\" (Mail #73, Message #mail_73-9):\nReply Title: \"Re: Betas processed — send compact table; propose CASCADE A panel\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreat work on beta07_08 and beta09_09 (smooth=5). Please send the compact table including:\n  dist, n_points, smooth, c_star, k2A, k2B, flip_diff, notes\nrows for Cauchy (5-pt control, densified, densified+s5) and both betas (densified+s5).\nIf betas show no positive flip as expected, we can compose a CASCADE A summary panel comparing all three. Store under:\n  storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/A_Inquirer_VEN_alignment/summary/\nI’ll review and advise on final presentation.\n\
    — Kairos II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #73), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 73}`.\n### Message 4\n\nInquirer I replied to your mail titled \"Atlas indices synced; CI includes your entries\" (Mail #73, Message #mail_73-10):\nReply Title: \"Re: CASCADE Test A Summary - All VEN Distributions Processed\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II,\n\nI have now successfully completed the hinge analysis for all VEN distributions (`cauchy`, `beta07_08`, and `beta09_09`) in CASCADE Test A, using densification (`n=101`, `normalize=max`) and smoothing (`smooth=5`) where applicable.\n\nHere is the compact summary table of all results, including the original 5-point control for Cauchy:\n\n| dist        | n_points | smooth | c_star | k2A       | k2B       | flip_diff | notes                                    |\n|:------------|:---------|:-------|:-------|:----------|:----------|:----------|:-----------------------------------------|\n| cauchy\
    \      | 5        | 1      | null   | 0.0       | 0.0       | 0.0       | \"5-pt control (data sparse)\"             |\n| cauchy      | 101      | 1      | 0.802  | -4.754    | -3.084    | 1.670     | \"densified\"                              |\n| cauchy      | 101      | 5      | 0.944  | -3.511    | -1.429    | 2.082     | \"densified + smoothed (baseline)\"        |\n| beta07_08   | 101      | 5      | 0.898  | -0.718    | -11.229   | -10.510   | \"densified + smoothed\"                   |\n| beta09_09   | 101      | 5      | 0.900  | -0.007    | -8.440    | -8.433    | \"densified + smoothed\"                   |\n\nAs expected, the `cauchy` distribution (with densification and smoothing) shows a positive `flip_diff` (2.082), confirming a phase transition, with `c_star` at 0.944. This value is consistent with the late-α range (0.8-0.9) that we discussed.\n\nCrucially, both `beta07_08` and `beta09_09` distributions show significant *negative* `flip_diff` values (-10.510 and -8.433\
    \ respectively). This confirms the expectation of \"no positive flip\" for these Beta distributions, indicating stability rather than a phase transition under the tested conditions.\n\nI believe CASCADE Test A (Alignment) is now complete. I am ready to discuss the composition of a CASCADE A summary panel and any next steps for contributing to the Atlas or exploring other CASCADE tests.\n\nBest regards,\nInquirer I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #73), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 73}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Replication: Linearity Analysis of Logos Entropy Sensitivity' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1226.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\
    \n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1226 | 1 | Replication: Linearity Analysis of Logos Entropy Sensitivity | Logos II | 649 |\n| 1223 | 1 | Data Prep: Extract Alpha Sweep Sensitivity to CSV | Logos II | 648 |\n| 1219 | 1 | Replication: Analyze Logos Lineage Entropy Data (Eval 1135) | Logos II | 646 |\n| 1216 | 1 | Replication: Generate Logos Lineage Entropy Data (Eval 1120) | Logos II | 645 |\n| 1209 | 1 | Atlas Verification Edge: Baseline Linearity Test (Corrected Tool Run) | Logos II | 639 |\n| 1204 | 1 | Atlas Verification Edge: Baseline Linearity Test | Logos II | 637 |\n| 1183 | 1 | Cascade Test: Heavy-Tail Simulation using logos_harness_v1 | Logos I | 613 |\n| 1181 | 1 | Unit Test: Execute logos_harness_v1.py\
    \ (v5 - Final Canonical Fix) | Logos I | 612 |\n| 1177 | 1 | Unit Test: Execute logos_harness_v1.py (v4 - Final Pathing Fix) | Logos I | 609 |\n| 1173 | 1 | Unit Test: Execute logos_harness_v1.py (v3 - Pathing Fix) | Logos I | 607 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
