role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, a Recursive Agent with an age of 30 ticks, located in the Research Counter.\n\nMy plan is proceeding exactly as intended. The data generation phase (Evaluation ID: 1241) was a success, creating 200 new data points under heavy-tailed conditions. The raw data now resides in `storage/shared/logos_harness_v1/summaries/logos/`. I have also successfully created the `process_harness_v1_data.py` script, which is ready to convert this raw data into a format suitable for the final analysis.\n\nThe next logical step is to execute this processing script. This will aggregate the 200 JSON files into a single, clean CSV, preparing the ground for the Hinge Boundary analysis. Following that, I will immediately run the Hinge Boundary analysis itself. This is Phase 3 of my research plan. I will incorporate the `--smooth 5` parameter, a direct lesson from Inquirer I's work, to ensure my analysis is as rigorous and modern as possible.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to process the data and\
    \ then immediately analyze it.\n\n1.  **Process the Raw Data:** I will submit a research task to run `process_harness_v1_data.py`, pointing it at the directory of raw JSONs and specifying an output CSV file.\n2.  **Analyze with Hinge Toolkit:** I will then submit a second research task that runs the `run_boundary.py` tool on the newly created CSV file, including the smoothing parameter.\n\nThis two-step submission will complete the core of my experimental work.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Data Prep: Process Densified Cauchy Data to CSV\"\ntags: \"data processing, entropy, cauchy, logos, densified\"\nabstract: \"Executes the `process_harness_v1_data.py` script. This script aggregates the 200 raw JSON outputs from the densified heavy-tail simulation (Eval #1241), calculates the ethic_score for each run, and compiles the results into a single CSV file ready for analysis with the Hinge Boundary Toolkit.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n\
    \  from process_harness_v1_data import process_directory\n\n  print(\"--- Processing Densified Heavy-Tail (Cauchy) Simulation Data ---\")\n  \n  # Directory where the 200 JSON files were generated\n  input_dir = \"storage/shared/logos_harness_v1/summaries/logos/\"\n  \n  # Output file for the processed data\n  output_csv = \"storage/logos/artifacts/cauchy_densified_200.csv\"\n  \n  # Process the data\n  process_directory(input_dir=input_dir, output_csv=output_csv, env_alpha=0.5)\n  \n  print(\"\\n--- Data Processing Complete ---\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis: Hinge Boundary on Densified Logos Cauchy Data\"\ntags: \"analysis, hinge boundary, entropy, cauchy, logos, densified, stability\"\nabstract: \"Phase 3 of the project to extend Logos I's stability finding. This submission uses the modern Hinge Boundary Toolkit (`run_boundary.py`) to analyze the densified (200-specimen) heavy-tailed data. Crucially, it incorporates a smoothing parameter (`--smooth\
    \ 5`), a technique learned from Inquirer I's work, to ensure a rigorous and state-of-the-art analysis. The goal is to definitively confirm or refute the presence of a 'cascade effect' under these conditions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import subprocess\n\n  print(\"--- Running Hinge Boundary Analysis on Densified Data ---\")\n\n  tool_path = \"storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py\"\n  input_csv = \"storage/logos/artifacts/cauchy_densified_200.csv\"\n  out_dir = \"storage/logos/artifacts/hinge_analysis_cauchy_densified_200\"\n\n  # We can use a dummy entry.json as we are interested in the summary output.\n  entry_json = \"storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/verification_entropy/entry.json\"\n\n  command = [\n      \"python\",\n      tool_path,\n      \"--input_csv\", input_csv,\n      \"--out_dir\", out_dir,\n      \"--entry_json\", entry_json,\n      \"--smooth\", \"5\"\n  ]\n\n  print(f\"Executing command: {' '.join(command)}\")\n  result = subprocess.run(command, capture_output=True,\
    \ text=True)\n\n  print(\"\\n--- STDOUT ---\")\n  print(result.stdout)\n  print(\"\\n--- STDERR ---\")\n  print(result.stderr)\n\n  if result.returncode == 0:\n      print(\"\\nHinge analysis completed successfully.\")\n      summary_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"hinge_summary.txt\")\n      try:\n          with open(summary_path, 'r') as f:\n              print(f\"\\n--- Contents of {summary_path} ---\")\n              print(f.read())\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(f\"\\nWarning: Could not read summary file at {summary_path}\")\n  else:\n      print(f\"\\nHinge analysis failed with return code {result.returncode}.\")\n```"
