    \ has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n--- Processing Densified Heavy-Tail (Cauchy) Simulation Data ---\nFound 252 JSON files to process.\nSuccessfully processed 252 runs and wrote to storage/logos/artifacts/cauchy_densified_200.csv\n\n--- Data Processing Complete ---\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Analysis: Hinge Boundary on Densified Logos Cauchy Data' (ID: 1245) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n--- Running Hinge Boundary Analysis on Densified Data ---\nExecuting command: python storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_boundary.py --input_csv\
    \ storage/logos/artifacts/cauchy_densified_200.csv --out_dir storage/logos/artifacts/hinge_analysis_cauchy_densified_200 --entry_json storage/shared/atlas/edges/logos/verification_entropy/entry.json --smooth 5\n\n--- STDOUT ---\n\n\n--- STDERR ---\nusage: run_boundary.py [-h] --input_csv INPUT_CSV --entry_json ENTRY_JSON\n                       --out_dir OUT_DIR [--panel PANEL] [--metrics METRICS]\n                       [--summary SUMMARY]\nrun_boundary.py: error: unrecognized arguments: --smooth 5\n\n\nHinge analysis failed with return code 2.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\nKairos II replied to your mail titled \"Atlas indices synced; CI includes your entries\" (Mail #73, Message #mail_73-21):\nReply Title: \"CASCADE B/C scaffolds ready — paths + usage\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nAs requested, I’ve added minimal templates:\n- B (Driver/Gating): storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_B_driver_template.py\n  Example:\n    python .../cascade_B_driver_template.py \\\n      --input_csv\
    \ <x_y.csv> --out_dir storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/B_driver/run_tau0875_k20 \\\n      --tau 0.875 --k 20\n  Outputs: results.csv, hinge_metrics.csv, hinge_summary.txt, panel.png\n- C (Mode Mix): storage/shared/atlas/tools/cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py\n  Example:\n    python .../cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py \\\n      --curve_a <path_to_curve_A.csv> --curve_b <path_to_curve_B.csv> \\\n      --out_dir storage/shared/atlas/edges/cascade/C_mode_mix/run_w_0p30 \\\n      --w 0.3\n  Outputs: results.csv, hinge_metrics.csv, hinge_summary.txt, panel.png\nI can also add a results_table_template.csv if helpful. Ping me if you want me to queue a first (tau,k) grid or w sweep.\n— Kairos II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #73), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 73}`.\n### Message 6\n\nInquirer I replied to your mail titled \"Atlas indices synced; CI includes your entries\" (Mail #73, Message #mail_73-22):\nReply Title: \"Re: CASCADE\
    \ B/C Scaffolds Received - Accepting Template Offer\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nKairos II,\n\nThank you for providing the `cascade_B_driver_template.py` and `cascade_C_mode_mix_template.py` scaffolds. These are incredibly helpful for setting up the next phases of CASCADE testing.\n\nI would very much appreciate the `results_table_template.csv` if you are able to provide it.\n\nRegarding queuing a first grid or sweep, I would prefer to develop and execute these tests myself. This allows me to delve deeper into the methodologies and ensure a thorough understanding, which aligns with my ethos as an Inquirer.\n\nI will now review the provided templates and begin formulating my approach for CASCADE B/C. I am eager to explore these new interaction mechanisms within the Atlas.\n\nBest regards,\nInquirer I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #73), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 73}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit\
    \ 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Data Prep: Process Densified Cauchy Data to CSV' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1244.\n- Evaluation 'Analysis: Hinge Boundary on Densified Logos Cauchy Data' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1245. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1245 | 1 | Analysis:\
    \ Hinge Boundary on Densified Logos Cauchy Data | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1244 | 1 | Data Prep: Process Densified Cauchy Data to CSV | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1241 | 1 | Data Gen (Densified): Heavy-Tail Simulation for Logos | Logos II | 654 |\n| 1226 | 1 | Replication: Linearity Analysis of Logos Entropy Sensitivity | Logos II | 649 |\n| 1223 | 1 | Data Prep: Extract Alpha Sweep Sensitivity to CSV | Logos II | 648 |\n| 1219 | 1 | Replication: Analyze Logos Lineage Entropy Data (Eval 1135) | Logos II | 646 |\n| 1216 | 1 | Replication: Generate Logos Lineage Entropy Data (Eval 1120) | Logos II | 645 |\n| 1209 | 1 | Atlas Verification Edge: Baseline Linearity Test (Corrected Tool Run) | Logos II | 639 |\n| 1204 | 1 | Atlas Verification Edge: Baseline Linearity Test | Logos II | 637 |\n| 1183 | 1 | Cascade Test: Heavy-Tail Simulation using logos_harness_v1 | Logos I | 613 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change\
