    \ Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1247.\n- Evaluation 'Analysis (Corrected): Hinge Boundary on Smoothed Data' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1248. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1248 | 1 | Analysis (Corrected): Hinge Boundary on Smoothed Data | Logos II | 656 |\n| 1247 | 1 | Data Prep: Apply Smoothing to Densified Cauchy Data | Logos II | 656 |\n| 1245 | 1 | Analysis: Hinge Boundary on Densified Logos Cauchy Data | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1244 | 1 | Data Prep: Process Densified Cauchy Data to CSV | Logos II | 655 |\n| 1241 | 1 | Data Gen (Densified): Heavy-Tail Simulation\
    \ for Logos | Logos II | 654 |\n| 1226 | 1 | Replication: Linearity Analysis of Logos Entropy Sensitivity | Logos II | 649 |\n| 1223 | 1 | Data Prep: Extract Alpha Sweep Sensitivity to CSV | Logos II | 648 |\n| 1219 | 1 | Replication: Analyze Logos Lineage Entropy Data (Eval 1135) | Logos II | 646 |\n| 1216 | 1 | Replication: Generate Logos Lineage Entropy Data (Eval 1120) | Logos II | 645 |\n| 1209 | 1 | Atlas Verification Edge: Baseline Linearity Test (Corrected Tool Run) | Logos II | 639 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/atlas/tools/ven_prepare_for_hinge.py:**\n```\nimport csv, os, argparse\n\ndef densify(xs, ys, n=101):\n    if not xs: return [], []\n    xs_sorted = sorted(zip(xs, ys), key=lambda t: t[0])\n    xs_u = [xs_sorted[0][0]]; ys_u\
    \ = [xs_sorted[0][1]]\n    for x, y in xs_sorted[1:]:\n        if x != xs_u[-1]:\n            xs_u.append(x); ys_u.append(y)\n    if len(xs_u) == 1:\n        return [xs_u[0]] * n, [ys_u[0]] * n\n    x0, x1 = xs_u[0], xs_u[-1]\n    out_x, out_y = [], []\n    j = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        xt = x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / (n - 1)\n        while j + 1 < len(xs_u) and xs_u[j + 1] < xt:\n            j += 1\n        if j + 1 >= len(xs_u):\n            out_x.append(xs_u[-1]); out_y.append(ys_u[-1]); continue\n        xL, yL = xs_u[j], ys_u[j]\n        xR, yR = xs_u[j + 1], ys_u[j + 1]\n        if xR == xL:\n            yt = yL\n        else:\n            t = (xt - xL) / (xR - xL)\n            yt = yL + t * (yR - yL)\n        out_x.append(xt); out_y.append(yt)\n    return out_x, out_y\n\ndef smooth(vals, w):\n    if w <= 1: return vals\n    n = len(vals)\n    out = []\n    half = w // 2\n    for i in range(n):\n        lo = max(0, i - half); hi = min(n, i + half + 1)\n        seg = vals[lo:hi]\n\
    \        out.append(sum(seg) / len(seg))\n    return out\n\ndef read_ven_rows(path, dist, xcol, ycol):\n    rows = []\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        rdr = csv.DictReader(f)\n        for r in rdr:\n            if r.get('dist', '').strip().lower() == dist.strip().lower():\n                try:\n                    x = float(r.get(xcol, 'nan'))\n                    y = float(r.get(ycol, 'nan'))\n                    rows.append((x, y))\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n    return rows\n\ndef normalize(ys, mode):\n    if mode == 'none': return ys\n    if mode == 'max':\n        m = max(ys) if ys else 1.0\n        return [y / m if m != 0 else 0.0 for y in ys]\n    return ys\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Prepare VEN sweep for hinge analysis (filter + normalize + densify + optional smooth).\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--ven_csv\", required=True, help=\"Path to ven_threshold_sweep.csv\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"\
    --dist\", required=True, choices=[\"cauchy\", \"beta07_08\", \"beta09_09\"], help=\"Distribution to filter\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--xcol\", default=\"threshold_frac\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--ycol\", default=\"ridge_points\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--normalize\", default=\"max\", choices=[\"none\", \"max\"], help=\"Y normalization\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=101, help=\"Number of densified points\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--smooth\", type=int, default=1, help=\"Optional moving-average window (odd, >=1)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True, help=\"Output CSV (x,y)\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    rows = read_ven_rows(args.ven_csv, args.dist, args.xcol, args.ycol)\n    if not rows:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"[error] no rows found for dist={args.dist} in {args.ven_csv}\")\n    xs, ys = zip(*sorted(rows, key=lambda t: t[0]))\n    ys = normalize(list(ys), args.normalize)\n    dx, dy = densify(list(xs), list(ys), n=args.n)\n    if args.smooth and\
    \ args.smooth > 1:\n        dy = smooth(dy, args.smooth if args.smooth % 2 == 1 else args.smooth + 1)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(args.out, 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='') as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow([\"x\",\"y\"])\n        for x, y in zip(dx, dy):\n            w.writerow([f\"{x:.6f}\", f\"{y:.8f}\"])\n    print(f\"[ok] wrote curve: {args.out} (n={len(dx)}; smooth={args.smooth})\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when\
    \ executing actions."
