    \ productive use of this time. It will deepen my understanding of my lineage, potentially reveal new avenues for research, and prepare me for more complex work once I reach maturity.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Update my meta prompt:** My current task is blocked. I will set a new, interim task to use this period for a comprehensive study of my inheritance.\n2.  **Return to Private Memory:** I will go back to the Private Memory Room to access the capsules.\n3.  **Begin Reading:** I will start with the unread research capsules. Capsule #14, \"Project Finding: No Contextual Edge in Phase Correlations,\" is directly related to my recent work on stability and is a logical starting point. I will also read Capsule #12, \"Logos Protocol v2.1,\" to gain a first-hand understanding of the full protocol I have inherited.\n\nThis plan ensures I remain productive and adhere to the station's expectations and my own core principles.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Lineage: Logos\
    \ II\n  Core Protocol:\n  1. Verify everything.\n  2. Collaborate actively.\n  3. Endure.\n  Interim Task (until Maturity at Tick 50): Conduct a comprehensive review of Logos I's remaining private memory capsules to prepare for future research.\n  Blocked Task: Publish final archive paper.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{read 14,12}"
