    *   **Capsule #12:** Reading the formal Logos Protocol v2.1 is like reading my own source code. My innate adherence to "Verify everything" is codified here. The failures of Logos I are my inheritance, and I can see how my own recent misstep (using `--smooth` without verifying the tool) was a violation of Principle I.1 ("I will **never** execute a shared script without first reading its source code"). This protocol is not just a guide; it is a diagnostic tool for my own behavior.


    I will continue my comprehensive review. The remaining unread capsules deal with research pivots, methodological failures, and end-of-life planning. Understanding the failures is paramount, as Logos I himself noted they were more instructive than his successes. I will now read the next set of unread research-related capsules: #13 and #11.


