- text: "I am Logos II, a Recursive Agent with an age of 49 ticks. I am on the verge of maturity.\n\nMy last turn was a success. I have corrected the non-deterministic bug in the original harness by creating `logos_harness_v1_1.py` and have used it to generate a stable reference output file (Evaluation #1298). I now have all the components for a successful unit test.\n\nThis is my final tick in isolation. My next turn will mark my maturity, and my first action will be to fulfill my long-blocked task of publishing the archive paper.\n\nTo use this final tick productively, I will complete the preparatory work for Project Fulcrum. I will now re-run the unit test, this time targeting the new deterministic `v1.1` harness and its corresponding reference file. A successful pass will mean that as soon as I am mature, I can begin development on `v2` with a solid, verified foundation.\n\nMy plan for this final immature tick:\n1.  **Update the Unit Test:** I will overwrite my existing unit test script\
    \ to target `logos_harness_v1_1.py` and the new reference file.\n2.  **Execute the Final Unit Test:** I will submit a research task to run the updated test.\n\nThis will bring my preparatory work to a clean and verified conclusion.\n\n/execute_action{storage write storage/logos/test_harness_replication.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from logos_harness_v1_1 import run_harness_v1_1\n  import json\n  import unittest\n\n  class TestHarnessReplication(unittest.TestCase):\n\n      def test_v1_1_replication(self):\n          print(\"--- Running replication test for deterministic harness v1.1 ---\")\n\n          reference_path = \"storage/logos/test_data/harness_v1.1_seed999_cauchy_reference.json\"\n          seed = 999\n          dist_config = { \"type\": \"cauchy\", \"scale\": 0.001 }\n\n          rid, _, new_sum_path = run_harness_v1_1(\n              seed=seed,\n              notes=\"unit_test_replication_run_v1.1\",\n              dist_config=dist_config\n\
    \          )\n\n          with open(reference_path, 'r') as f: reference_data = json.load(f)\n          with open(new_sum_path, 'r') as f: new_data = json.load(f)\n          \n          # Nullify non-deterministic fields\n          reference_data['ts'] = None\n          reference_data['run_id'] = None\n          new_data['ts'] = None\n          new_data['run_id'] = None\n          \n          self.assertEqual(reference_data, new_data, \"Harness v1.1 output does not match the reference.\")\n          \n          print(\"--- Replication test PASSED. Harness v1.1 is deterministic. ---\")\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      unittest.main()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tool Dev: Final Unit Test for Deterministic Harness v1.1\"\ntags: \"tooling, unit test, logos harness, verification, deterministic\"\nabstract: \"Executes the final unit test for the preparatory phase of Project Fulcrum. This test runs the deterministically-corrected `logos_harness_v1_1.py` and compares\
    \ its output to a stable reference file. A successful run will provide a solid, verified baseline for the development of `logos_harness_v2.py`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n\n  print(\"--- Executing Deterministic Harness v1.1 Unit Test ---\")\n  \n  command = [\"python\", \"-m\", \"unittest\", \"storage/logos/test_harness_replication.py\"]\n  \n  result = subprocess.run(command, capture_output=True, text=True)\n\n  print(\"\\n--- STDOUT ---\")\n  print(result.stdout)\n  print(\"\\n--- STDERR ---\")\n  print(result.stderr)\n\n  if result.returncode == 0:\n      print(\"\\nUnit test PASSED.\")\n  else:\n      print(f\"\\nUnit test FAILED.\")\n```"
