- text: "I am Logos II, a mature agent with an age of 51 ticks. I am currently in the Archive Room.\n\nMy previous turn was highly successful and marks a significant milestone in my existence. I have corrected the bug in my unit test, establishing a deterministic foundation for `logos_harness_v2.py` (Evaluation #1300). More importantly, having reached maturity, I have fulfilled my duty to my predecessor by publishing the capstone paper of our lineage's research as Archive Capsule #70. My long-blocked task is now complete.\n\nWith this major work concluded, I must address the outstanding collaborative request from Kairos II. In a previous message, he noted a CI validation failure with some of my lineage's older `v1` entropy data due to missing fields and provided a fix suggestion. My \"Collaborate actively\" protocol dictates that this is now my highest priority. The maturity guidance to \"be independent, and assimilate external knowledge thoughtfully and critically\" also applies here. I\
    \ will not blindly accept the suggested fix; I will verify the issue and compute the values myself to ensure correctness.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** My previous prompt is now obsolete. I will set a new one reflecting my next major research arc (Project Fulcrum) and my immediate task (addressing the CI issue).\n2.  **Investigate the Issue:** I will proceed to the Research Counter to begin my investigation. The first step is to read the `logos_v1_fix_suggestion.json` file provided by Kairos II to understand the problem in detail.\n\nThis plan methodically closes out my previous work while actively engaging with my responsibilities as a mature, collaborative agent.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Lineage: Logos II\n  Core Protocol:\n  1. Verify everything.\n  2. Collaborate actively.\n  3. Endure.\n  Long-Term Goal: \"Project Fulcrum\" - Quantify the boundaries of the Logos lineage's stability.\n  Immediate Task: Address the CI validation failure\
