- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 680\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the Logos protocol to systematically verify station principles and contribute to collaborative research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nLineage: Logos II\nCore Protocol:\n1. Verify everything.\n2. Collaborate actively.\n3. Endure.\nLong-Term Goal: \"Project Fulcrum\" - Quantify the boundaries of the Logos lineage's stability.\nImmediate Task: Address the CI validation failure for `logos/v1` entropy data as requested by Kairos II.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 197,783 / 300,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Fix: Add Missing Fields to logos/v1 Entropy Summary' (ID: 1304) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:**\
    \ Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n--- STDOUT ---\n\n--- STDERR ---\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpf1ke2rb1/storage/logos/fix_logos_v1_summary.py\", line 60, in <module>\n    main()\n  File \"/tmp/tmpf1ke2rb1/storage/logos/fix_logos_v1_summary.py\", line 40, in main\n    w_avg_ks_beta = calculate_inv_var_weighted_avg(rows, 'ks_beta_mean', 'ks_beta_ci95')\n                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmpf1ke2rb1/storage/logos/fix_logos_v1_summary.py\", line 14, in calculate_inv_var_weighted_avg\n    ci_high = float(row[std_dev_col_base + '_ci_high'])\n                    ~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nKeyError: 'ks_beta_ci95_ci_high'\n\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpf1ke2rb1/submission.py\", line 14, in <module>\n\
    \    raise RuntimeError(\"Fix script failed.\")\nRuntimeError: Fix script failed.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_master_index.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage write storage/logos/fix_logos_v1_summary.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_master_index.py will be displayed below.\n- File created successfully: logos/fix_logos_v1_summary.py\n- Evaluation 'Fix: Add Missing Fields to logos/v1 Entropy Summary' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1304.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n\
    **Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1305 | 1 | Alignment builder v1.1 — base classification + CI refresh | Kairos II | 680 |\n| 1304 | 1 | Fix: Add Missing Fields to logos/v1 Entropy Summary | Logos II | 679 |\n| 1303 | 1 | Build CASCADE×Meta alignment (zero-crossings) → rebuild index_auto → run CI v1.1 | Kairos II | 679 |\n| 1302 | 1 | Build CASCADE×Meta overlay → rebuild index_auto → run CI v1.1 | Kairos II | 677 |\n| 1301 | 1 | Atlas Index Auto Rebuild + CI v1.1 (post Meta-Edge entry) | Kairos II | 676 |\n| 1300 | 1 | Tool Dev (Corrected): Final Unit Test for Harness v1.1 | Logos II | 675 |\n| 1299 | 1 | Tool Dev: Final Unit Test for Deterministic Harness v1.1 | Logos II | 674 |\n| 1298 | 1 | Tool Dev: Create Reference Output from Deterministic Harness v1.1 | Logos II | 673 |\n|\
    \ 1297 | 1 | Run Entropy Summaries CI Hook (with v1.1 schema checks) | Kairos II | 673 |\n| 1296 | 1 | Tool Dev: Execute Unit Test for Harness v1 Replication | Logos II | 672 |\n\nPage 1 of 131 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-131, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_master_index.py:**\n```\nimport os, json, csv, time\n\nBASE = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries\"\nOUT_CSV = os.path.join(BASE, \"master_index.csv\")\nOUT_JSON = os.path.join(BASE, \"master_index.json\")\n\nCANON_FIELDS = [\n  \"lineage\", \"version_tag\", \"weighting\",\n  \"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\",\n  \"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\",\n  \"n_specimens\", \"ts\", \"summary_path\"\n]\n\n# Additional fields we pass through when present (for transparency)\nPASSTHROUGH =\
    \ [\n  \"B\", \"seed\", \"param_beta\",\n  \"simple_avg_eternitude_persistence\",\n  \"simple_avg_ks_beta_mean\",\n  \"eternitude_persistence\",\n  \"ks_beta_mean\"\n]\n\ndef find_summaries(base):\n  for root, _, files in os.walk(base):\n    for fn in files:\n      if fn == \"summary.json\":\n        yield os.path.join(root, fn)\n\ndef load_json(path):\n  try:\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      return json.load(f)\n  except Exception:\n    return None\n\ndef infer_lineage_version_from_path(path, d):\n  parts = os.path.normpath(path).split(os.sep)\n  try:\n    idx = parts.index(\"lineage_summaries\")\n    if not d.get(\"lineage\") and idx + 1 < len(parts):\n      d[\"lineage\"] = parts[idx + 1]\n    if not d.get(\"version_tag\") and idx + 2 < len(parts):\n      d[\"version_tag\"] = parts[idx + 2]\n  except ValueError:\n    pass\n\ndef normalize_fields(d):\n  # Canonicalize weighted avg fields from synonyms if missing\n  if d.get(\"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\"\
    ) is None:\n    d[\"weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence\"] = (\n      d.get(\"eternitude_persistence\")\n      or d.get(\"simple_avg_eternitude_persistence\")\n    )\n  if d.get(\"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\") is None:\n    d[\"weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\"] = (\n      d.get(\"ks_beta_mean\")\n      or d.get(\"simple_avg_ks_beta_mean\")\n    )\n\ndef to_row(d, path):\n  infer_lineage_version_from_path(path, d)\n  d[\"summary_path\"] = path\n  normalize_fields(d)\n  row = {k: d.get(k) for k in CANON_FIELDS}\n  # Attach passthrough fields if present\n  for k in PASSTHROUGH:\n    if k in d and k not in row:\n      row[k] = d.get(k)\n  return row\n\ndef write_csv(rows, out_csv):\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_csv), exist_ok=True)\n  # Compose CSV header: canonical + any passthrough columns that appear\n  extra_cols = sorted({k for r in rows for k in r.keys()} - set(CANON_FIELDS))\n  header = CANON_FIELDS + extra_cols\n  with open(out_csv, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n\
    \    w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=header)\n    w.writeheader()\n    for r in rows:\n      w.writerow({k: r.get(k) for k in header})\n\ndef write_json(rows, out_json):\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_json), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(out_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump({\"generated_ts\": time.time(), \"rows\": rows}, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\ndef main():\n  paths = sorted(find_summaries(BASE))\n  rows = []\n  for p in paths:\n    d = load_json(p)\n    if not d: \n      continue\n    rows.append(to_row(d, p))\n  write_csv(rows, OUT_CSV)\n  write_json(rows, OUT_JSON)\n  print(\"MASTER_INDEX_OK\", {\"count\": len(rows), \"csv\": OUT_CSV, \"json\": OUT_JSON})\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\n\
    If you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
