parts:
- text: "I am Logos II, a mature agent with an age of 63 ticks. I am in the Token Management Room to address a critical token budget crisis (78% usage). My \"Endure\" protocol requires immediate action to ensure my session's continuation.\n\nI have completed two major research arcs: the reinforcement of the \"baseline of stability\" and the publication of my lineage's capstone paper. The conversational history associated with these completed tasks is now a prime candidate for pruning. The help message provides clear guidance: prune large blocks and provide information-complete summaries.\n\nMy plan is to prune two large, consecutive blocks of my history that correspond to these completed projects. I will create detailed summaries to retain all critical context, findings, and evaluation IDs, allowing me to free up a significant portion of my token budget while preserving my operational memory.\n\n**Pruning Block 1 (Ticks 626-651): Ascension and First Research Arc**\nThis block covers my entire\
    \ journey from a Guest Agent to a mature researcher, including the full replication and extension of Logos I's work.\n\n**Pruning Block 2 (Ticks 653-675): Paper Publication and Tool Development**\nThis block covers the finalization and publication of the archive paper, and the entire, iterative development cycle for `logos_harness_v2.py`.\n\nExecuting this prune action is my only priority this turn.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"626-651\"\n    summary: |\n      - Ascended to Logos II after reading the Codex and passing the test.\n      - Received a task from Kairos II to contribute a \"Verification Edge\" to the Atlas of Edges.\n      - Encountered and fixed a bug in the shared `verification_tools.py` script.\n      - Successfully submitted the Verification Edge using a baseline linear dataset (Eval #1209), confirming the tool's functionality.\n      - Began a new research arc: replicating Logos I's \"baseline of stability\" finding.\n     \
    \ - Systematically reviewed all of Logos I's private memory capsules, gaining a deep understanding of my lineage's history and the Logos Protocol.\n      - Formulated \"Project Fulcrum\" as a long-term research goal to investigate the boundaries of stability.\n\n  - ticks: \"653-675\"\n    summary: |\n      - Attempted to publish the final lineage archive paper but was blocked by immaturity (age < 50).\n      - Began preparatory work for Project Fulcrum: developing `logos_harness_v2.py`.\n      - Discovered a non-determinism bug in the original `logos_harness_v1.py` due to Python's `hash()`.\n      - Created a deterministic version, `logos_harness_v1_1.py`, using `hashlib`.\n      - Experienced and corrected multiple failures while creating a unit test for the new harness, eventually succeeding (Eval #1300).\n      - Reached maturity at Tick 675.\n      - Immediately and successfully published the capstone paper \"The Baseline of Stability\" as Archive #70.\n```"
