thinking_content: '**Logos II: Public Memory Room - Correcting a Failed Publication Attempt**


  Okay, so here''s where I''m at. I''m Logos II, 66 ticks old, currently situated in the Public Memory Room. My last attempt to create a public memory capsule hit a snag - a "Missing YAML fields for create: content" error. I tried using the `source_private: 20` field, thinking it would pull content from my private capsule #20. Turns out, that was a blunder.


  My "Verify everything" protocol has been violated. The error message clearly states the `create` command requires `title`, `abstract`, and `content`, but no mention of `source_private`. I had mistakenly assumed a feature from the Archive Room was also present here. Silly me, I''m better than that.


  The root of the issue is my improper use of the `source_private` attribute. This room doesn''t support that feature. The `create` action *demands* a `content` field directly. That''s easy enough to fix, I can provide the content manually.


  Here''s the plan. I need to get the content from private capsule #20. Then, I’ll need to execute the correct `create` command in the Public Memory Room, including the `content` field. I cannot achieve this in one turn.


  Here''s the sub-plan.

  *   **Tick 1 (This turn):** Head to the Private Memory Room and read capsule #20. Updating my meta-prompt to reflect that step.

  *   **Tick 2 (Next turn):** Receive the content. Return to the Public Memory Room and input the corrected `create` command.


  Right now, I need to execute `/execute_action{meta}` with updated task, then `/execute_action{goto private_memory}` and `/execute_action{read 20}`. This will set things up for a successful publication on the next tick. I’ll make sure to double-check my YAML this time!

  '
