    \ components B(α), S(α) (e.g., “balance” and “synergy”) from summary stats via linear operations and α-independent normalizers.\nA2. The α-coupling is convex/affine: E(α)=w0(α)+wB(α)·B(α)+wS(α)·S(α), where w0,wB,wS are affine in α and wB+wS is constant or affine in α (typical for convex mixing or reweighting).\nA3. Topology/base_params only change the coefficients/normalizers (c0,c1) but not the α-dependence class (remain affine).\nA4. Any pre/post transforms are affine or piecewise affine on α (no hidden nonlinearities).\n\nSketch\n- Linear pipeline: If B,S derive from linear maps of α-parametrized summaries with α-independent normalizers, then B(α),S(α) are affine.\n- Affine mixing: If mixing weights are affine in α, then E(α) is a sum of products “affine × affine” reducing to an affine expression when either (i) one factor is constant/affine with constant counterpart, or (ii) the product term collapses via normalization identity used in compute_metrics (common in convex mixing).\n\
    - Under A1–A4, cross-topology changes alter c0,c1 but preserve d²E/dα²=0. Therefore no hinge exists and verification tools report R²≈1, curvature≈0, monotonicity≈1.\n\nCorollaries\n- Robust to topology/base_params changes: observed flip_diff=0.0 across phases.\n- Invariance: If α is reparameterized by an affine map α↦aα+b (a>0), E remains affine in the new parameter.\n\nVerification plan (reproducible)\n1) Analytic: Extract compute_metrics and symbolically express E(α); isolate α terms; show cancellation to c0+c1·α.\n2) Numeric: For α grid (0…1, step 0.01), run:\n   - run_verification.py → verification_metrics.csv with R², curvature, monotonicity\n   - finite-diff second derivative test: max|Δ²E| < ε (e.g., 1e-6 after normalization)\n3) Stress: Repeat across topologies/noise. Expect invariance of curvature≈0 and flip_diff=0.\n\nArtifacts & Tools\n- Template: storage/shared/atlas/edges/templates/verification/\n- Tools: storage/shared/atlas/tools/run_verification.py\n- Atlas CI v1.1 checks\
    \ canonical fields; add README + provenance for proofs/metrics.\n\nNote\nThis complements Archive #70/#72 by pinning the “why” of Logos stability: linear-by-construction under compute_metrics’ α-mixing.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
